operation shadow legacy begins soon in  rainbow six siege  and it's bringing splinter cell sam  fisher into the fold  here's everything you need to know about  the new operator  sam fisher's rainbow six code name is  zero and as you'd probably expect  he's an attacker armed with an sc3000  assault rifle  mp7 and 5.7 usg he can also carry either  frag grenades or a claymore as his  secondary gadget  but what you really want to know about  is his operator gadget  the argus launcher this launches cameras  that can pierce through breakable and  reinforced surfaces  once the camera is mounted sam can  toggle it to look through either side of  the wall  the camera can also fire a single laser  shot which is powerful enough to destroy  operator gadgets  like alibi's prisma decoy  other players can mess with your camera  though it can be destroyed and mute can  jam it with his signal disrupters for  example  so as with any operator there's a give  and take with sam's special  ability he's the biggest addition to  siege in operation shadow legacy but  he's not the only change coming  defenders will be able to place more  reinforcements now  each player can place up to 4 walls from  a total pool of 10.  some attacking operators will also get a  new secondary gadget  the hard breaching round which can make  holes in reinforced walls  meanwhile thatcher is getting nerfed  specifically his emp  grenades will now only be able to  disable gadgets instead of destroying  them  lastly the chalet map is getting a  rework that sees many of its familiar  areas  changed so that's a whole lot of shake  up for the meta for the new season  and that's all you need to know before  you jump in stay tuned to gamespot for  more coverage of the new siege season  [Music]  you
 

